  "says": "The trance lead: one oscillator stacked into many detuned saw copies (seven is the classic count) spread across the stereo field, the detune wide enough that the copies beat into a shimmer rather than a chorus, a bright but not fizzy top, and a short attack so it hits on the beat. Wide, bright, harmonic, loud in the upper mids.",
